---
title: "lifecycle (LegionSealedBidAuctionSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_init: initialize(saleInitParams, auctionParams + ECIES publicKey)
    q_init --> q_active: Auction active - investors submit encrypted bids
    q_active --> q_ended: end() by LegionOrProject
    q_active --> q_canceled: cancel() by Project (whenCancelNotLocked)
    q_ended --> q_refundWindow: Refund period starts
    q_refundWindow --> q_refundOver: block.timestamp >= endTime + refundDuration
    q_refundOver --> q_initPublish: initializePublishSaleResults() locks cancel
    q_initPublish --> q_publish: publishSaleResults() reveals privateKey
    q_publish --> q_decryptable: All bids now decryptable via decryptSealedBid()
    q_decryptable --> q_claimable: Investors claim via Merkle proof
    q_claimable --> q_withdrawCapital: withdrawRaisedCapital() by Project
    q_withdrawCapital --> [*]: Complete
    q_canceled --> q_refundAll: withdrawInvestedCapitalIfCanceled()
    q_refundAll --> [*]: All capital returned

    note right of q_active
        INV-001: Bids encrypted with ECIES public key, amounts hidden on-chain
        INV-002: invest() stores encrypted bid, actual amount unknown until reveal
    end note

    note right of q_initPublish
        INV-003: Two-step publish prevents project cancel during result finalization
        INV-004: Cancel locked after initializePublishSaleResults()
    end note

    note right of q_publish
        INV-005: Private key must derive to stored public key
        INV-006: decryptSealedBid(encryptedAmountOut, investor) reveals bid post-publish
    end note
